    12	 * - `<!--`, which opens a comment inside a script element and makes the parser treat the remainder
    13	 *   up to `-->` as commented-out, so a bundle containing it would silently stop executing part-way.
    14	 *
    15	 * Both are escaped with a backslash, which JavaScript ignores before `/` and `!` but which stops the
